    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d509">

                <pb facs="0889" n="819" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg819"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to General
                        Salgar</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-12-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 29, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">General:</hi> I have received your note of the 22d
                    instant, requesting the surrender for trial by the tribunals of Colombia of the
                    marine attached to the United States steamer James Adger, who is charged with
                    killing, at Aspinwall, on the 10th of November, 1865, of one George Holmes,
                    alleged to be a British subject.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to state that in the absence of an extradition treaty between the
                    United States and the United States of Colombia, the request cannot, it is
                    conceived, be properly complied with.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of this occasion, general, to offer to you a renewed assurance of
                    my high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Señor General Don <hi rendition="#small-caps">Eustorjio Salgar</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
